# Context

## Why This Way
The runtime opens before setupTrial, not inside it: setup
failure must reuse finalizeSetupFailure, and the runtime's close
belongs to runTrial so every exit route (setup catch, session
catch, adapter throw, finalization) closes the child exactly
once after the final reads.

## Key Trade-offs
- Contract-mode artifacts stay byte-identical; scenario branches
  are additive (state.final/summary gain real values only when
  a runtime exists).
- Scenario reads happen between the adapter run and finalization,
  then the child closes; finalization works from captured facts,
  so a late artifact write cannot leak a live store.
- pack_id in the §25.7 record is the pack metadata name, per the
  SPEC example ("workspace-service"); backend.name reuses it.

## Gotchas
- semantic-events.redacted.jsonl is written only in scenario
  mode, empty file when a run commits no events.

